NAME

ulibAddFile - Adds an entry to the file catalogue


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibAddFile(struct CatCommand *NewFile)


DESCRIPTION

This function adds an entry to the file catalogue.

The following elements of the CatCommand structure are used:

   <File1>
        A pointer to the (struct FileCat) to be added.

        The file description (File1->Description) and file description length
        (File1->DescriptionLength) fields MUST be valid.

        The section to add the file to is taken from (File1->Section)

   <SubDir>
        The number of the file subdirectory (not to be confused with Section)
        in which the physical file resides; this parameter is required so that
        this function can auto-filenote the file with its description if
        the Sysop has configured Xenolink this way.

        If <SubDir> is negative one (-1), this function will search all
        subdirectories in the file's section.  If the physical file still
        cannot be found, the file will not be filenoted (of course), but the
        addition of the file to the catalogue will proceed normally.

   <Flags>
        Quick - If set, Xenolink will NOT check to see if the file already
                exists, but will instead add it to the catalogue right away.
                Do not use this option in a multi-node environment where other
                programs can change the catalogue without your notice; what was
                true a second ago may no longer be true!

                Xenolink uses this option internally when moving a file from
                one section to another (internally, the file is deleted from
                the catalogue and then added to a new section, as one atomic
                operation).


RETURNS

0        - Success
Non-zero - Failure, file already in catalogue
